WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.790
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:13.090
Last time: big job → small jobs

3
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:23.330
Chapter 5 · Capstone: Math Puzzle Challenge

4
00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:37.310
Capstone = the final challenge

5
00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:43.020
Grab a pencil. Puzzle time!

6
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:49.690
Meet Ishaan at the school Maths Mela!

7
00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:57.760
5 stations · 5 stars · 1 golden badge

8
00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:09.320
What could help when a puzzle feels hard?

9
00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:14.810
"Don't just guess. Pick a strategy!"

10
00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:17.710
Strategy = a plan for solving a problem

11
00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:27.590
Find the rule · Draw it · Break it · Go back

12
00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:39.330
Show your working, then check it

13
00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:53.690
2, 4, 6, 8, ___?

14
00:01:53.690 --> 00:01:59.960
10! Rule: add 2 each time

15
00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:11.780
1, 3, 6, 10, ___? Look at the jumps!

16
00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:26.360
+2, +3, +4, then +5 → 10 + 5 = 15

17
00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:38.000
Sort smallest to biggest: 45, 12, 30

18
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:45.830
12, 30, 45!

19
00:02:45.830 --> 00:03:02.610
Venn diagram: red things · fruits

20
00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:08.610
Where does a red apple go?

21
00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:16.290
The middle! Red AND a fruit

22
00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:23.960
Grid address = (across, up)

23
00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:33.260
(3, 1) → 3 across, 1 up

24
00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:47.590
Start (1, 1): 2 right, 3 up, 1 right. Where?

25
00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:59.260
Across 1 + 2 + 1 = 4 · Up 1 + 3 = 4 → (4, 4)

26
00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:09.500
Facing east. Half turn. Which way now?

27
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:15.060
West! A half turn faces the opposite way

28
00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:23.610
True or false? A coin lands heads for certain

29
00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:32.890
False! Heads or tails: about equally likely

30
00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:39.340
Impossible · Unlikely · Likely · Certain

31
00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:53.760
Priya bought 6 beads. Now 15. Start with?

32
00:04:53.760 --> 00:05:03.320
Draw it, then flip it: +6 becomes −6

33
00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:14.930
15 − 6 = 9 · Check: 9 + 6 = 15

34
00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:19.190
5 stars! The golden puzzle badge!

35
00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:25.040
Your maths helps computers and AI!

36
00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:36.380
Screens are grids: every pixel has an address

37
00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:47.950
AI uses probability to pick what's most likely

38
00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:51.960
Your turn: capstone check

39
00:05:51.960 --> 00:06:03.140
Name 2 maths ideas that help computers or AI

40
00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:19.610
Grids & coordinates · Probability

41
00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:24.210
Find the rule to continue a pattern

42
00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:26.880
Grid address = (across, up)

43
00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:31.440
Certain · Likely · Unlikely · Impossible

44
00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.570
Show your working and check it

45
00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:47.460
